# Vendored copies of the override patches isomer's consumers carry (the same
# files as examples/tools/patches): bzlmod applies a git_override's or a
# single_version_override's patches only from the MAIN repository, so every
# consumer keeps its own copy until the fixes are released upstream. Two for
# flatbuffers (the swift BUILD glob, WASI's Foundation shim), two for
# rules_swift (a wasi-threads SDK beside the single-threaded one; the Swift
# SDK's clang resource directory for C compiled for wasm). And the
# Playground's own: rules_swift_package_manager on Windows.
exports_files(glob(["*.patch"]))
